# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notary runtime artifacts
#
# The ledger database lives in SQLite; the -journal/-wal/-shm sidecars are
# written beside it. The gap log is a separate plain file by design (it exists
# to survive a store outage), so it is ignored here too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
notary-gaps.log

# The compiled binary, when built in the repo root with `go build`.
/notary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit key material
#
# Notary reads its signing key and the Mem0 API key from the ENVIRONMENT
# (NOTARY_SIGNING_KEY, NOTARY_MEM0_API_KEY). Nothing in this repo reads a .env
# file, so a stray one here would be both inert and committable. These rules
# exist so that mistake cannot reach a commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tool state (not part of the project)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.reasonix/
.superpowers/
.worktrees/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go build and test output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.test
*.out
/dist/
/bin/
go.work
go.work.sum
